      "notes": "<h2>🔴 WHAT: BUILDING YOUR BRIDGE PAGE</h2><p>In this lesson, we’ll create a <strong>bridge page</strong>, a simple web page that acts as a transition between someone clicking an ad or link and being directed to the sales page. This page builds curiosity, pre-sells the offer, and improves conversions.</p><hr><h2>🟠 WHY: THE IMPORTANCE OF A BRIDGE PAGE</h2><p>The bridge page has several critical functions:</p><ul><li><p>Helps pre-frame the offer for better engagement.</p></li><li><p>Provides a clean and concise introduction before the sales page.</p></li><li><p>Gives your audience a seamless transition, which increases trust and reduces bounce rates.</p></li></ul><blockquote><p>💡 <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> If you’re promoting a <strong>digital product</strong> with its own sales page, you can skip this step and proceed to the copy customization lesson.</p></blockquote><hr><h2>🟢 HOW: CREATING YOUR BRIDGE PAGE</h2><p>Here’s how to create your own bridge page effortlessly:</p><h3>STEP 1: REGISTER FOR A <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-[#C9A44C] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#C9A44C]/80\" href=\"https://www.gohighlevel.com/?fp_ref=justfunnel\">GO HIGH LEVEL</a> ACCOUNT</h3><p>If you haven’t already, <strong>sign up for a Go High Level account</strong>. This will act as the central hub for your operations and simplify the entire process of building and managing your pages.</p><h3>STEP 2: INSTALL THE BRIDGE PAGE TEMPLATE</h3><p>I’ve provided <strong>3 ready-made templates</strong> for bridge pages. Start by installing the <strong>single-section bridge page template</strong>. This is the simplest and fastest to use for your first setup.</p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-[#C9A44C] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#C9A44C]/80\" href=\"https://affiliates.gohighlevel.com/?fp_ref=gcooke&amp;funnel_share=69f87e75b69ddf739b2ab81d\">Bridge page 1</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-[#C9A44C] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#C9A44C]/80\" href=\"https://app.gohighlevel.com/v2/preview/wBbQ2hr4faJELOkcTqMO\">(preview)</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-[#C9A44C] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#C9A44C]/80\" href=\"https://affiliates.gohighlevel.com/?fp_ref=gcooke&amp;funnel_share=69f895bd671aafa949f64ff1\">Bridge page 2</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-[#C9A44C] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#C9A44C]/80\" href=\"https://app.gohighlevel.com/v2/preview/hZCPssLSlR2KE93oXAZD\">(preview)</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-[#C9A44C] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#C9A44C]/80\" href=\"https://affiliates.gohighlevel.com/?fp_ref=gcooke&amp;funnel_share=6a03667e09b7380096e9a894\">Bridge page 3</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-[#C9A44C] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#C9A44C]/80\" href=\"https://app.gohighlevel.com/v2/preview/d8TaQZIfLrApVDBjqjLm\">(preview)</a></p><p>The typical structure of the bridge page includes:</p><ul><li><p>An <strong>announcement bar</strong> at the top.</p></li><li><p>A bold <strong>headline</strong>.</p></li><li><p>A <strong>subheadline</strong> to expand on your headline's promise.</p></li><li><p>An <strong>image</strong> (or relevant visual).</p></li><li><p>A strong <strong>call-to-action button</strong> linking to the sales page.</p></li></ul><p>You can also see a list of templates here for 'advertorial' style bridge pages which are longer and more used on ads rather than content but can be used on both. These have a 30% CTR (click through rate) but warm the prospect up more than a normal style bridge page.</p><blockquote><p>⚡ <strong>Insight:</strong> There are two common types of bridge pages: a simple single-section page or an <strong>advertorial-style bridge page</strong>. The latter is more detailed, resembling a blog post, but links to the sales page in a similar way. For speed and simplicity, stick to the single-section template for now.</p></blockquote><h3>STEP 3: CONNECT YOUR DOMAIN</h3><p>Once the template is installed, you’ll need to <strong>connect a custom domain</strong>. This domain should relate to your offer for easy recognition. For example, if you’re promoting an AI-related product, choose a domain that reflects that niche.</p><p>You can use a <strong>Go High Level domain</strong> (recommended for ease of use) or purchase one from platforms like GoDaddy. After getting your domain:</p><ol><li><p>Follow the steps to connect it to Go High Level.</p></li><li><p>Ensure the domain feels relevant and professional - but don’t overthink or get stuck on this step!</p></li></ol><blockquote><p>🛠️ <strong>Tool Tip:</strong> To save time, use a domain service integrated with Go High Level. This ensures seamless setup without any complex configurations.</p></blockquote><hr><h2>🎯 NEXT UP: CUSTOMIZING YOUR COPY</h2><p>In the next lesson, we’ll focus on <strong>amending the copy</strong> for your bridge page. You’ll also learn to utilize the AI generator to craft compelling headlines and subheadlines that drive results.</p><blockquote><p>🔗 <strong>Resource:</strong> If you’re ready to move ahead, install your bridge page template from the provided resources below.</p></blockquote><p></p>",
