      "notes": "<h2>🔴 WHAT: ADDING IMAGES TO A BRIDGE PAGE</h2><p><strong>This lesson focuses on adding an image or GIF to your Bridge page</strong> to create curiosity and complement your headline. A pre-built Canva template is provided to make the process simple and efficient.</p><hr><h2>🟠 WHY: THE PURPOSE OF THE IMAGE</h2><p>The main purpose of the image or GIF on a Bridge page is to <strong>generate curiosity</strong>. It should align with the headline without giving away the full outcome. This subtle intrigue encourages the viewer to continue engaging with your content.</p><hr><h2>🟢 HOW: IMPLEMENTING THE IMAGE OR GIF</h2><h3>STEP 1: USE THE CANVA TEMPLATE</h3><p>To save time, use the provided <strong>Canva template</strong>. This template is designed specifically for Bridge pages and can be easily edited to suit your offer.</p><blockquote><p>🔗 <strong>Download the Canva template </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-[#C9A44C] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#C9A44C]/80\" href=\"https://canva.link/ylbuzs0cy9zarhg\"><strong>here</strong></a></p></blockquote><h3>STEP 2: MATCH THE HEADLINE</h3><p>Make sure your selected image or GIF <strong>matches the theme of your headline</strong>. The visual should complement the text and maintain curiosity without revealing too much.</p><h3>STEP 3: EXAMPLES PROVIDED</h3><p><strong>Examples of effective images and GIFs</strong> are included for reference. Feel free to use these directly or modify them as needed. If you're using one of our templates, a pre-built GIF with four fast images is already included on your Bridge page.</p><blockquote><p>💡 <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> You can also use AI tools to create quick and engaging images or GIFs if you’d like to customize further.</p></blockquote><h3>STEP 4: AVOID OVERTHINKING</h3><p>This process does not need to be complicated. If you're happy with the provided resources, <strong>stick with them and move forward</strong>. Spending too much time here can delay your progress, so keep it simple.</p>",
